WEBVTT

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:06.810
October 4, 1957: the first artificial satellite.

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:09.420
A beep that changed the world.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:17.920
Today, in Arequipa, the investors want results. The farmers want data on their crops.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:20.430
Goicochea wants both.

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:25.990
Chicho counts every gram. Roberto counts every byte.

00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:28.540
<v Chicho>Every gram we save is fuel we keep.

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.580
Flight one. Lost.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:41.070
The news asks if this is serious. Social media has jokes.

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:48.230
Flight two. Flight three. Lost. The money is almost gone.

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:50.870
<v Franchesca>We go again. One more time.

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:55.250
They were not the first to fail three times.

00:00:55.290 --> 00:01:00.860
In 2008, a small private rocket reached orbit on its fourth try.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.670
Flight four. Orbit.

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:07.370
<v Goicochea>Paulet... we are in orbit.

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:13.330
Now it's your turn: design the satellite that will not fail.

